WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.647
Practice 2 creates a patient-month admission matrix.

00:00:03.647 --> 00:00:06.667
The output grain is one row per patient.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:12.687
Month columns contain admission counts, and total admissions provides an overall measure.

00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:19.107
Because the query starts from patients with a left join, patients with no admissions are still represented.

00:00:19.107 --> 00:00:23.267
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:28.572
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:28.572 --> 00:00:31.992
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:31.992 --> 00:00:36.467
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:43.512
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:43.512 --> 00:00:47.467
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project:

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:51.874
validate the meaning of the result, not only whether the statement executes.
